{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2024 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "d3a87e8b6ffa24660e18d564e5c0a66d9fb93b851fa4da3eddb57dacbcd8729c" :edb/db-before-t 2023 :edb/db-after-t 2024 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535336 50 #inst "2026-10-08T22:20:35.999Z" 13194139535336 true] [17592186083115 1020 #edb/ref 17592186344290 13194139535336 true] [17592186083115 1020 #edb/ref 17592186344294 13194139535336 true] [17592186083116 1020 #edb/ref 17592186344297 13194139535336 true] [17592186083255 1020 #edb/ref 17592186344280 13194139535336 true] [17592186083255 1020 #edb/ref 17592186344287 13194139535336 true] [17592186344280 1017 #edb/ref 17592186344281 13194139535336 true] [17592186344280 1089 "q-152779" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344280 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535336 true] [17592186344280 1100 "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6}{(z+2)^{4}}\\,\\text{d}z.$" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344280 1113 #uuid "2bdb7d52-6816-5912-9b60-a3ec899e692c" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344280 1145 "First, we substitute $u=z+2.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}z}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{d}z.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to \\infty $ when $z\\to \\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=z+2$ is as follows:\n\n| $z$ | $-1$ | $\\infty $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $\\infty $ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6}{(z+2)^{4}}\\,\\text{d}z={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6}{{u}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}u\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6}{(z+2)^{4}}\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6}{{u}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{u}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}{u}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{3}{u}^{-3}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{{u}^{3}}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\frac{1}{{a}^{3}}-\\frac{1}{{1}^{3}}] \\\\  & =-2\\cdot (0-1) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344281 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344282 13194139535336 true] [17592186344281 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344283 13194139535336 true] [17592186344281 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344284 13194139535336 true] [17592186344281 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344285 13194139535336 true] [17592186344281 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344286 13194139535336 true] [17592186344281 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535336 true] [17592186344281 1041 "selection" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344281 1104 #edb/ref 17592186344285 13194139535336 true] [17592186344281 1110 #uuid "a7af7e8f-410f-5568-b4b7-4ff308fc9746" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344282 1034 "The integral diverges" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344282 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535336 true] [17592186344282 1111 #uuid "7837b34f-2f07-5eb6-bb96-40fc9c40bacf" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344283 1034 "3" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344283 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535336 true] [17592186344283 1111 #uuid "12f87729-5188-5272-a77b-3ec75fe4c548" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344284 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344284 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535336 true] [17592186344284 1111 #uuid "788b2813-f86c-592d-ae92-b9ba3f8d43bf" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344285 1034 "2" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344285 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535336 true] [17592186344285 1111 #uuid "2d4af8ae-06d1-5267-b6bb-a7b51c84c0cd" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344286 1034 "\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344286 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535336 true] [17592186344286 1111 #uuid "9b12a8a8-2a3d-5bb4-8175-8631655f718b" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344287 1017 #edb/ref 17592186344288 13194139535336 true] [17592186344287 1089 "q-350530" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344287 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535336 true] [17592186344287 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{5}{(3y+2)^{4}}\\,\\text{d}y=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344287 1113 #uuid "8ae06e11-3b4b-55e3-b2a5-df274e7748c0" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344287 1145 "First, we substitute $u=3y+2.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}y}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=3\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to \\infty $ when $y\\to \\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=3y+2$ is as follows:\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $\\infty $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $\\infty $ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{5}{(3y+2)^{4}}\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{5}{3{u}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}u\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{5}{(3y+2)^{4}}\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{5}{3{u}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{5}{3}{u}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{2}^{a}\\frac{5}{3}{u}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{5}{9}{u}^{-3}]}_{2}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{9}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[{u}^{-3}]}_{2}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{9}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\frac{1}{{a}^{3}}-\\frac{1}{{2}^{3}}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{9}\\cdot (0-\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{72}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344289 13194139535336 true] [17592186344288 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535336 true] [17592186344288 1041 "field-1" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344288 1104 #edb/ref 17592186344289 13194139535336 true] [17592186344288 1110 #uuid "992bab60-b4dd-5f0b-8e4f-9e0847c08eff" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344289 1034 "\\frac{5}{72}" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344289 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535336 true] [17592186344289 1111 #uuid "b2c3c665-cc9a-5fff-8971-f38b9bf3a039" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344290 1017 #edb/ref 17592186344291 13194139535336 true] [17592186344290 1089 "q-350537" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344290 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535336 true] [17592186344290 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{10}{{x}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344290 1113 #uuid "cda1b2de-8da8-517b-8487-2e8df17cbd49" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344290 1145 "We proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{10}{{x}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}x & =10{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{-1}{x}^{-6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =10{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{-5}]}_{a}^{-1} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}]}_{a}^{-1} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\frac{1}{(-1)^{5}}-\\frac{1}{{a}^{5}}] \\\\  & =-2\\cdot (-1-0) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344291 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344292 13194139535336 true] [17592186344291 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344293 13194139535336 true] [17592186344291 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535336 true] [17592186344291 1041 "field-1" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344291 1104 #edb/ref 17592186344292 13194139535336 true] [17592186344291 1110 #uuid "17eae316-3906-51b2-9fb9-d1269dd02d65" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344292 1034 "2" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344292 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535336 true] [17592186344292 1111 #uuid "b759741e-626a-55a5-900e-5ca9e82faa79" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344293 1034 "-2" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344293 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535336 true] [17592186344293 1111 #uuid "5e50c56f-77c5-5a66-b782-c86e1ab0654a" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344294 1017 #edb/ref 17592186344295 13194139535336 true] [17592186344294 1089 "q-350540" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344294 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535336 true] [17592186344294 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{6}{(2x+1)^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344294 1113 #uuid "57d778df-49ba-5f2a-8974-783c558a308f" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344294 1145 "First, we substitute $u=2x+1.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=2\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to -\\infty $ when $x\\to -\\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=2x+1$ is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $-\\infty $ | $-1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-\\infty $ | $-1$ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{6}{(2x+1)^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{3}{{u}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}u\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{3}{{u}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}u & =3{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{-1}{u}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{3}{u}^{-3}]}_{a}^{-1} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{1}{{u}^{3}}]}_{a}^{-1} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\frac{1}{(-1)^{3}}-\\frac{1}{{a}^{3}}] \\\\  & =-(-1-0) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344295 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344296 13194139535336 true] [17592186344295 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535336 true] [17592186344295 1041 "field-1" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344295 1104 #edb/ref 17592186344296 13194139535336 true] [17592186344295 1110 #uuid "86451857-4f62-5366-a9bb-5f09fd21119e" 13194139535336 true] [17592186344296 1034 "1" 13194139535336 true] [175921